<item>
            <title>[LU-20917] find in-kernel RDMA headers in Debian</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20917</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The DKMS config detects in-kernel o2ib support by checking for&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;rdma_cm.h, ib_cm.h and ib_verbs.h under ${kernel_source_dir}/include/rdma.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On Debian, the kernel headers are split into an arch-specific package&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;and a &quot;-common&quot; package, and the generic include/ tree (including&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;include/rdma) lives only in the latter, under&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;/usr/src/linux-headers-&amp;lt;version&amp;gt;-common. Since the arch-specific&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;directory has no include/rdma, can_o2ib_in_kernel stays &quot;no&quot; and the&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;in-kernel o2ib stack is never detected, so ko2iblnd is not built.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; modprobe: FATAL: Module ko2iblnd not found in directory&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; /lib/modules/&amp;lt;kernel-version&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&#160; &#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Search both ${kernel_source_dir} and&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;/usr/src/linux-headers-${kernelver%-*}-common for the RDMA headers,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;and set can_o2ib_in_kernel=yes as soon as a directory contains all&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;three.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
